WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.266
Hi, I'm Tangerine!

00:00:02.266 --> 00:00:06.497
A swarm of agents can ask a decision model everything in one call.

00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:09.100
Here's how, and where the teamwork really lives.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.085
The expensive half of a decision is the state.

00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:17.340
Ten agents looking at one world send ten questions against one copy of it.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.801
Ten snakes share one arena.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:27.404
Before anything is asked, code measures every move: food distance, reachable cells, dead-end risk.

00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:31.601
Each tick sends one request: the state once, plus ten short questions.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.748
Ten answers come back in roughly the time of one.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.357
Each snake gets its own probabilities.

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:40.275
By design, no question can see another's answer.

00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:45.462
So coordination happens in code: a resolver enumerates joint moves, drops illegal

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:49.434
ones, and keeps the likeliest, in about half a millisecond.

00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:53.333
How often it overrules the model is the honest diagnostic.

00:00:54.967 --> 00:00:57.263
A live tick in the project's own app.

00:00:57.263 --> 00:01:00.707
Four snakes are still alive, and four questions went in one request.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:05.485
This tick's decisions: each snake gets its own move, with its own probability.

00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:09.260
And the override rate the README calls its Go or No-Go gate:

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.379
two point two percent.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.603
Grouped against one shared state, the choice readout barely moved: two hundred

00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:19.201
sixty-nine of two hundred seventy answers agreed.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:23.260
The score readout, a weighted mean over a rubric, shifted about zero

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.472
point two nine levels.

00:01:24.472 --> 00:01:27.505
The winner survives a shift that a mean does not.

00:01:28.808 --> 00:01:32.575
A batch shares the state, not the answers: coordination is code, and

00:01:32.575 --> 00:01:34.773
only the score readout shows the drift.

00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:40.451
To recap: share the state, resolve in code, and check the scores.

00:01:41.542 --> 00:01:43.774
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:43.774 --> 00:01:44.412
I'm Tangerine.

00:01:44.412 --> 00:01:44.731
Bye!
